From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 08:05:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] view: A window moved to another screen is scaled for that
 screen

A window moved to the phone took its new size while it still had its old
position: the commit updated the size first. Scale-to-fit therefore judged
the phone's window height against the desktop's usable area, shrank the
window and arranged it on the desktop again, so that it hung across both
screens. The position is now updated first.

The maximized box also divided its position by the view's scale. Positions
are layout coordinates; with a screen away from the origin and a scale
below 1 the window landed elsewhere, and the geometry offset went the wrong
way. It stayed unnoticed with one screen, at the origin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/view.c         | 9 +++++----
 src/xdg-toplevel.c | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/view.c b/src/view.c
index 1d6969d..a7a762b 100644
--- a/src/view.c
+++ b/src/view.c
@@ -873,8 +873,9 @@ phoc_view_get_maximized_box (PhocView *self, PhocOutput *output, struct wlr_box
   usable_area.x += output_box.x;
   usable_area.y += output_box.y;
 
-  box->x = usable_area.x / priv->scale;
-  box->y = usable_area.y / priv->scale;
+  /* The position is in layout coordinates, only the size scales */
+  box->x = usable_area.x;
+  box->y = usable_area.y;
   box->width = usable_area.width / priv->scale;
   box->height = usable_area.height / priv->scale;
 
@@ -895,8 +896,8 @@ view_arrange_maximized (PhocView *self, PhocOutput *output)
     return;
 
   phoc_view_get_geometry (self, &geom);
-  box.x -= geom.x / priv->scale;
-  box.y -= geom.y / priv->scale;
+  box.x -= geom.x * priv->scale;
+  box.y -= geom.y * priv->scale;
 
   phoc_view_move_resize (self, box.x, box.y, box.width, box.height);
 }
diff --git a/src/xdg-toplevel.c b/src/xdg-toplevel.c
index b16a480..9f6b271 100644
--- a/src/xdg-toplevel.c
+++ b/src/xdg-toplevel.c
@@ -466,8 +466,8 @@ handle_surface_commit (struct wl_listener *listener, void *data)
 
   struct wlr_box size;
   get_size (view, &size);
-  view_update_size (view, size.width, size.height);
 
+  /* The position first: the new size is judged on the screen the view is going to */
   uint32_t pending_serial = self->pending_move_resize_configure_serial;
   if (pending_serial > 0 && pending_serial >= xdg_toplevel->base->current.configure_serial) {
     double x = view->box.x;
@@ -491,6 +491,8 @@ handle_surface_commit (struct wl_listener *listener, void *data)
       self->pending_move_resize_configure_serial = 0;
   }
 
+  view_update_size (view, size.width, size.height);
+
   struct wlr_box geometry;
   phoc_xdg_toplevel_get_geometry (self, &geometry);
   if (self->saved_geometry.x != geometry.x || self->saved_geometry.y != geometry.y) {
